# ABB M1M.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | ABB M1M — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: abb-m1m-modbus-manual.pdf
# | - Applies to M1M 15, M1M 20, M1M 20 Pro, M1M 30, M1M 30 Pro.
# | - 3-phase energy and power quality meter, panel-mount, RS485 Modbus RTU.
# | - Holding registers FC03 (all measurement/energy registers are read-only).
# | - "Start Reg (Hex)" is the raw protocol address — NOT 40000-based, NOT decremented by 1.
# | - All multi-register values: Big-Endian (MSW first); no word_order needed.
# | - Size 1 register = 16-bit (u16/s16), Size 2 = 32-bit (u32/s32), Size 4 = 64-bit (u64/s64).
# | - Factory defaults: slave=1, configurable baud, 8N1.
# | - Note: "Current N" and THD registers only available on M1M 20/30 variants.
# | - Note: Unbalance registers only available on M1M 30 and M1M 20 I/O Pro.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=ABB
@model=M1M
@vendor_website=abb.com
@description=3-phase energy and power quality meter — system total + per-phase V/I/P/Q/S/PF/angle, frequency, CosPhi, 64-bit energy, THD (M1M 20/30), unbalance (M1M 30) (FC03, Big-Endian, 0x5Bxx instantaneous, 0x50xx energy).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/abb-m1m.toml; Source: abb-m1m-modbus-manual.pdf. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

